She anointed her face with ointment,
and she gathered the locks of her hair with a headdress;
she accepted a new dress in order to deceive him.

Her sandals ravished his eyes;
her beauty made his soul her captive;
with a blade, she cut off his head.

Woe to the people that rises up against my people.
For the Lord almighty will be vindicated against them;
in the day of judgment, he will visit them.

You have made known to me the ways of life;
you will fill me with joy by your countenance.
At your right hand are delights, even to the end.

He has placed his tabernacle in the sun,
and he is like a bridegroom coming out of his bedroom.
He has exulted like a giant running along the way;

Do not draw me away together with sinners;
and let me not perish with those who work iniquity,
who speak peacefully to their neighbor, yet evils are in their hearts.

I will exult and rejoice in your mercy.
For you have looked upon my humility;
you have saved my soul from needfulness.

He has been considering iniquity on his bed.
He has set himself on every way that is not good;
moreover, he has not hated evil.

So then, truly man passes by like an image;
even so, he is disquieted in vain.
He stores up, and he knows not for whom he will gather these things.

In the daylight, the Lord has ordered his mercy;
and in the night, a canticle to him.
With me is a prayer to the God of my life.

Understand these things, you who forget God;
lest at any time, he might quickly take you away,
and there would be no one to rescue you.

the earth was moved,
for the heavens rained down before the face of the God of Sinai,
before the face of the God of Israel.

A Psalm of Asaph. O God, the Gentiles have entered into your inheritance;
they have polluted your holy temple.
They have set Jerusalem as a place to tend fruit trees.

For even the lawgiver will provide a blessing;
they will go from virtue to virtue.
The God of gods will be seen in Zion.

In the morning, he may pass away like grass;
in the morning, he may flower and pass away.
In the evening, he will fall, and harden, and become dry.

And may the splendor of the Lord our God be upon us.
And so, direct the works of our hands over us;
direct even the work of our hands.

as in the provocation, according to the day of temptation in the wilderness,
where your fathers tempted me;
they tested me, though they had seen my works.

Moab is the cooking pot of my hope.
I will extend my shoe in Idumea;
the foreigners have become my friends.

They have hands, and do not feel;
they have feet, and do not walk.
Neither will they cry out with their throat.

Do not turn aside my heart to words of malice,
to making excuses for sins, with men who work iniquity;
and I will not communicate, even with the best of them.
